u-&gt;dg: submitBalance(accountId, amount)
dg-&gt;dc: updateBalance(accountId, amount)
dc-&gt;ac: updateBalance(amount)
dc-&gt;db: saveAccount(account)
db--&gt;dc: confirmation
dc--&gt;dg: display updated balance
u-&gt;dg: addCategory(name, balance)
dg-&gt;dc: createCategory(name, balance)
dc-&gt;cat: new Category(name, balance)
dc-&gt;db: saveCategory(category)
db--&gt;dc: confirmation
dc--&gt;dg: display new category
u-&gt;eg: submitExpense(amount, description, date)
eg-&gt;ec: recordExpense(data)
ec-&gt;ai: categorizeExpense(expense)
ai-&gt;px: generateResponse(request)
px--&gt;ai: AIResponse
ai--&gt;ec: suggested Category
ec--&gt;eg: show suggested category
u-&gt;eg: confirmCategory(category)
eg-&gt;ec: assignCategory(expense, category)
ec-&gt;ex: new Expense(amount, date, category)
ec-&gt;db: saveExpense(expense)
db--&gt;ec: confirmation
ec--&gt;eg: display updated expense
</panel_attributes><additional_attributes/></element>
<element><id>UMLNote</id><coordinates><x>20</x><y>875</y><w>1875</w><h>126</h></coordinates><panel_attributes>Alternative flows
- Non-numeric balance or category balance: user is asked to enter a valid number. Negative balances are accepted.
- AI cannot categorize or is unavailable: user picks the category manually.
- User rejects the AI category: user selects another.
- Database save fails: user is told the information could not be saved.
- CategoryGroup.add() is used when a category is placed inside a group (Composite).</panel_attributes><additional_attributes/></element>
